/*****************************************************************************
    jitSelfFn -- THE SHAPE THAT EXITED 139. A DRIVER WITH A PREAMBLE ABOVE A
    SELF-CALLING CALLEE, ITS GUARD RESET INSIDE THE DRIVER. 2026-08-05.

    ⚠ THIS IS incant/inlineSelfT's CRASHING HALF, PROMOTED FROM A BY-HAND
    RECIPE TO A RUNNABLE FIXTURE. inlineSelfT could only carry it as prose --
    rule H5, a fixture that dies takes every check below it with it -- and the
    reason it could not run was the defect S3 removes.

    THE DEFECT IT PINS. Emit-on-walk INLINES an ordinary callee into the
    caller's builder, so before S3 a self-call inside that inlined body had no
    separate function to name and got the ENCLOSING one:

        %selfcall = call i32 @jitFn0()      <- @jitFn0 IS THE DRIVER

    which re-enters the driver's ENTRY BLOCK and replays its whole preamble on
    every recursion. With the preamble harmless that is invisible; with the
    preamble holding the loop guard's reset, the guard is restored on every
    recursion and the recursion never ends. Exit 139, no degrade message, and
    no output after `jitRunAction: entering`.

    ⚠ WHY inlineSelfT's OWN GREEN HALF COULD NOT SEE IT, AND WHY displayForm
    COULD NOT EITHER: dfDrive's body is exactly ONE statement, so re-entering
    the whole function happened to equal re-entering the callee. Rung JC was
    green for a reason true of ITS DRIVER rather than of the mechanism -- the
    same class as `continue` appearing to work because both arms fell to the
    back edge. A driver with a preamble is the NORMAL case, and precisely the
    shape genParse's emitted rules will have.

    WHAT IS ASSERTED HERE, and none of it is an absence check (rule H4):

      rbCount  = 4   the number of ACTIVATIONS. Non-zero on purpose: a result
                     slot that merely defaults to zero cannot produce it, and a
                     preamble that replayed its `rbDepth = 3` would never stop
                     counting at all.
      rbOut    = 3   the OUTERMOST activation's local, read AFTER the recursive
                     call returns. Per-activation storage gives 3; aliased slots
                     give 0, because the innermost activation would have written
                     the shared slot last. Same discrimination J-R and jitJRL
                     use, one level further out.
      PREAMBLE = 1   printed ONCE. This is the other half of the defect and it
                     was the oddity recorded-but-not-chased on 2026-08-05: a
                     print in a driver ABOVE an inlined call produced NO output
                     in the jitted half while the oracle printed it once. Under
                     the replay it is 0 or N, never 1, so ONE is the only value
                     that distinguishes a driver preamble that ran exactly as
                     written from either failure.

    ⚠ H7 NEGATIVE CONTROL -- THE PRE-S3 BINARY IS THE KNOWN-DEFECTIVE SPECIMEN.
    This fixture is not a claim that would hold whatever the mechanism did: run
    it on a binary built before S3 and it does not merely disagree, it never
    returns. That is why the ladder runs it under a wall-clock cap and reports a
    timeout BY NAME rather than as a diff -- a killed process yields truncated
    output, and a truncation diff names the wrong row.

    ⚠ AND THE IR CARRIES THE SIGNATURE DIRECTLY (rider R3), which is stronger
    than the values because it names the mechanism rather than its consequence:
    NO function may contain a call to ITSELF unless it is the callee's own
    function. Before S3 the driver's function called itself; after S3 the driver
    calls the CALLEE's function and only the callee calls itself.

    ONE testing(), THEN jitRefire() FOREVER -- a second testing() on one action
    is the sequential-state-corruption tar baby, and the rung shape makes that
    unconstructable rather than merely avoided.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT, and exactly ONE stop() in this file (rule H2): a
    second stop() anywhere above it silently deletes everything between.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(SelfFn);
define
    sfDepth;
    sfArg;
    sfOut;
    sfCount;
    /*  THE CALLEE. It mentions its own name, so an inlined copy of it calling
        itself is the discovery S3's map is populated by.  */
    sf argument code={
        sfLoc = sfDepth;
        if sfDepth > 0;
            sfDepth = sfDepth - 1;
            sf(argument);
        sfCount = sfCount + 1;
        sfOut = sfLoc;
        };
    /*  ⚠ THE DRIVER'S PREAMBLE IS THE WHOLE FIXTURE. Two statements above the
        call, and the first of them is the loop guard's reset -- the exact
        placement inlineSelfT identified as the discriminating variable:
            guard reset OUTSIDE the driver -> nothing harmful replays -> exit 0
            guard reset INSIDE  the driver -> the reset replays forever -> 139
        Only the location of one statement differed there. Here it is inside.  */
    sfDrive code={
        sfDepth = 3;
        print "PREAMBLE":;
        sfOut = sf(sfArg);
        };
    ;

sfArg   = 7;
sfCount = 0;

print "== jitted: driver WITH a preamble above a self-calling callee ==":;
testing(sfDrive);

print "SF jitted : count = " sfCount " out = " sfOut:;

print "jitSelfFn SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
